        "thinking": "The `pathToRegex` function at line 147 generates `^${pattern}$` which requires an exact match. So for the path `/api/companies/`, the regex would be `/^\\/api\\/companies\\/$/`.\n\nBut the request is to `/api/companies` (no trailing slash), so it won't match `/api/companies/`.\n\nThat's the bug! The companies router registers `GET \"/\"`, and with prefix `/api/companies` becomes `/api/companies/`. But the request URL is `/api/companies` without the trailing slash.\n\nFix: normalize the path — either strip trailing slash from extracted route paths, or make the regex tolerate an optional trailing slash.\n\n\nI can see two approaches here. I could normalize paths in `extractRoutesFromRouter` by stripping trailing slashes from combined paths (except for the root), or I could modify `pathToRegex` to make the trailing slash optional in the regex pattern.\n\nActually, the cleanest solution is to normalize trailing slashes consistently—both when extracting routes and when matching requests. Let me update the route extraction logic to strip trailing slashes from constructed paths.",
